  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "On the Imperial Court battlefield, Hao Ji Liu as Water Demon names Wind Demon Tan Wu Feng after a four-leaf wind blade returns to its master. The two are called wind and water demons, both at rank four upper stage. Water Demon had rampaged in the eastern areas of Northern Plains while Wind Demon wreaked havoc in the western areas. Dong Fang Yu Liang devised three escapements scheme to subdue Wind Demon. Tan Wu Feng became Dong Fang Yu Liang’s subordinate and sided with Dong Fang tribe.",
      "chapters": [
        510
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_imperial_court",
        "char_hao_ji_liu",
        "reg_northern_plains",
        "char_dong_fang_yu_liang",
        "fac_dong_fang_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He is clothed in green, hovers in midair, and grasps the returning wind blade. Normally wind blades cannot be retrieved once sent. He pours in primeval essence so the damaged three-sided blade recovers to four leaves, then fights Hao Ji Liu as wind and water clash.",
      "chapters": [
        510
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He is clothed in green clothes, hovering in midair, grasping the wind blade that has returned.",
      "chapters": [
        510
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "After the Imperial Court contest, Wind Demon Tan Wu Feng remains with Dong Fang Yu Liang. Hao Ji Liu went to Hei Lou Lan and died. Tan Wu Feng converted from demonic to righteous as a subordinate of Dong Fang tribe’s previous leader. At Tai Qiu he wants to stay behind and stall a myriad beast goat group so his allies can escape. A blinding flash appears, and Dong Fang Yu Liang, Tan Wu Feng, and Dong Po Kong vanish from their spots.",
      "chapters": [
        781
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "tai-qiu-retreat",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "evt_arc_imperial_court_contest",
        "char_hei_lou_lan",
        "loc_tai_qiu",
        "char_dong_po_kong"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Old Lord Can Yang ignites Tan Wu Feng and Dong Po Kong on the spot, then enlarges the fire. Yellow -green flames roast these two rank five Gu Masters. They scream and collapse, but they cannot die. Gu Masters at rank five are at the peak of the mortal world, yet in front of Old Lord Can Yang they are completely controlled.",
      "chapters": [
        786
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fire-torment",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_old_lord_can_yang",
        "char_yellow",
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A huge flame turns Tan Wu Feng and Dong Po Kong into charcoal. Both are rank fives at the peak of the mortal world, killed in an instant.",
      "chapters": [
        787
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
